# Slice 5 · Live RAG · Ask My Company · Draft Reply · Pipeline Hardening

*pgvector + paragraph chunking + grounded answers · drafts replace canned strings · BackgroundTask safety net · OCR deferred*

---

## Why

Slice-2 made three product promises in mocked form: organize, ask, draft. Slice-3 made invoice organize REAL. Slice-4 made classify+summarize+review REAL on docs of every type. Slice-5 is when *ask* and *draft* stop being mocks. After this, the entire demo is grounded in actual AI working over the customer's actual documents — no canned strings hiding behind any UI surface.

Two new product moments land:
- A user types "Which invoices are due this week?" and gets a real answer citing real source filenames from their own corpus.
- A client request email gets a Romanian draft reply written by the LLM using the company's docs as context (not a canned string from `replies.ts`).

One quiet architectural move lands too: pipeline hardening. Slice-4's `_dedup_list set()→list` bug stayed silent because the BackgroundTask wrapper had no top-level exception handler — contracts sat at status="queued" forever. We add the safety net before any new code goes through the pipeline.

OCR is *deferred until pilot demand*. Image-only PDFs continue to flag `ocr_required` cleanly; we wait for a real user to ask before building the OCR layer.

---

## Scope

```
IN     pipeline hardening      app/services/analysis.py outer try/except around the BackgroundTask body
                                on unexpected exception: append AuditEvent("pipeline_failed:<step>",
                                {error, traceback_summary}) · set Document.status="failed"
                                no silent crashes · no docs stuck at status="queued"

       pgvector enabled        infra/docker-compose.yml: postgres image with pgvector preinstalled
                                (e.g., pgvector/pgvector:pg16) · alembic upgrade enables extension
                                schema: document_chunks(id, document_id FK, chunk_index, content TEXT,
                                                        embedding VECTOR(N), metadata JSONB, created_at)
                                ivfflat or hnsw index on embedding column

       chunking + embedding    app/services/chunking.py · paragraph chunker (split on blank-line)
                                                       · soft min/max chunk length · falls back to
                                                       sentence chunking if a single paragraph is too long
                                app/services/embeddings.py · OpenAI-compat client (env: EMBEDDING_MODEL)
                                                            · embed(text) and embed_batch([text])
                                                            · stays inside the provider adapter pattern

       new analyzer            DocumentIndexer · applies_to=ALL · runs LAST in registry order
                                chunks(rawText) → embed_batch → upsert into document_chunks
                                idempotent: deletes existing chunks for the doc before inserting fresh ones

       Ask My Company live     POST /api/ask {query: str} → AskAnswer (synchronous)
                                pipeline: embed query → pgvector cosine top-K=5 → build prompt with
                                          retrieved chunks (cite source filename per chunk) → LLM call →
                                          parse AskAnswer schema → save PromptRun (document_id null) → return
                                prompt: ask_company v1 · template from codocz §19.19 (literal preserve)
                                schema: AskAnswer (answer, source_documents, confidence, missing_information,
                                                   recommended_next_action, requires_human_review)
                                /app/ask: replace static qa.ts with real API call · loading state · source pills

       Draft Reply live        DraftReplyGenerator analyzer · applies_to={"client_request"}
                                runs in normal analyzer pipeline after upload
                                may retrieve top-3 chunks from the user's other docs as company context
                                prompt: email_reply_draft v1 · template from codocz §19.18
                                schema: DraftReply (detected_language, reply_subject, reply_body,
                                                    assumptions, missing_information, human_review_required,
                                                    recommended_next_action)
                                /app/inbox client_request detail: replace replies.ts canned reply with
                                                                    analyzer_outputs.draft_reply_generator content
                                Approve/Edit-locally/Discard UX unchanged from slice-2 (no Send button · ever)

       eval extension          tests/evals/fixtures/ask_questions.py · 5 fixtures from codocz §23.3
                                  example questions list · each carries: query · expected source filenames
                                  (set) · expected keywords in answer · "no relevant docs" cases for the
                                  fallback path
                                tests/evals/fixtures/draft_reply.py · 1 fixture (apartament email) ·
                                  expected: detected_language=ro · reply_body asks for floor plan / budget /
                                  start date · no commitments invented
                                runner extended to score Ask outputs (source-citation correctness · keyword
                                presence) and DraftReply outputs (assumption containment · human_review=true)

       seed extension          seed_demo.py adds: email_client_apartament_bucuresti  (so Draft Reply has a
                                                  client_request to chew on)
                                7-doc baseline → 8 docs · the additional 8 slice-2-mock docs that aren't
                                in the seed yet stay deferred (they're available as static demo content;
                                expand on pilot demand)

       env additions           .env.example: EMBEDDING_MODEL · EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS (defaults to provider's)
                                pgvector index parameters tunable later

       UI polish               /app/ask: input + send button + chat-style message list + source pills →
                                          card link to /app/inbox?focus=<doc_id>
                                /app/inbox client_request: Live badge on Draft Reply panel when
                                                            analyzer_outputs.draft_reply_generator present
                                                            (otherwise hide the panel rather than show canned)
                                image-only PDF surface: clearer audit-event message in UI ·
                                                       "PDF requires OCR — deferred until pilot demand"

OUT    OCR                                       deferred · awaits pilot demand · no work this slice
       multi-tenant / auth                       post-MVP
       conversation memory in /app/ask           later · single-question-single-answer for now
       streaming responses                       later
       reranking · hybrid search · query expansion later
       re-embedding on prompt version change     later · slice-N when prompts evolve
       chunk-version awareness                   later
       agentic / multi-step ask                  later
       Send button anywhere                      ever
```

