## Acceptance

```
hardening      kill the LLM provider connection mid-analysis → pipeline catches the exception ·
               document.status moves to "failed" · audit row "pipeline_failed:<step>" written ·
               the next valid upload still processes correctly (no stuck state)

pgvector       SELECT * FROM pg_extension WHERE extname='vector' returns a row
               document_chunks table exists · embedding column type vector(N)
               after seed: each document has at least 1 chunk row · embeddings populated

indexer        new uploads create chunks idempotently · re-uploading same doc replaces chunks
               (delete-then-insert) · DocumentIndexer registered last in ANALYZERS

ask live       POST /api/ask {"query":"Which invoices are due this week?"}
                 → 200 · answer cites at least one of the seeded invoice filenames ·
                   confidence in {"low","medium","high"} · prompt_run row recorded
               POST /api/ask {"query":"What did we agree about Antarctica?"}
                 → 200 · answer == "Information not found in your documents" · source_documents=[]
                   · confidence="low" · requires_human_review accordingly
               UI /app/ask: 8 §23.3 example questions render plausible answers with source pills
                 (does not need verbatim match — RAG is fuzzy · keyword presence + correct sources is the bar)

draft live     upload email_client_apartament_bucuresti as client_request →
                 ~10s later: analyzer_outputs.draft_reply_generator populated with reply_body in Romanian
                 reply asks for missing details (floor plan / photos / style / budget / start date)
                 no invented commitments · no concrete prices unless they exist in seeded docs
                 human_review_required=true
               UI /app/inbox client_request detail: Draft Reply panel shows the live draft ·
                 Live badge present · Approve/Edit-locally/Discard work as in slice-2 · NO Send button

eval           uv run python -m app.evals.run
                 ask_questions fixtures: source-citation correctness ≥80% · keyword presence ≥70%
                 draft_reply fixture: human_review_required=true · no commitments · score ≥7
                 invoice_extractor PO-reference fixture: still intentionally fails (regression catcher intact)
                 contract_reviewer 10/10 (regression check)

honesty        no hallucinated answers · ever · "not found" answers preferred over confident wrong ones
               source_documents only contains filenames that were actually retrieved from the corpus
               draft replies do not invent prices, contacts, or commitments not in the corpus
```

