## Constraints inherited

See `ops/rules.constraints.hybrid` (anchored). Slice-5 specific reinforcement:
- Provider adapter: embeddings calls go through the same `app/services/llm.py`-style adapter pattern. NEW adapter file `app/services/embeddings.py` is permitted — it should be the only place that imports the embedding-side SDK.
- Inline prompt version line on every NEW prompt template (ask_company v1 · email_reply_draft v1).
- The Ask My Company prompt template (§19.19) and Email Reply Draft prompt (§19.18) are LITERAL — copy the body verbatim from codocz/romanian_sme_ai_companion_prompt_pack.md to preserve the calibrated wording. Do NOT paraphrase.
- Pipeline hardening must NOT swallow expected analyzer failures — only catch unexpected exceptions (TypeError, OSError, etc). Pydantic ValidationError is still caught at the analyzer level and recorded as `analysis_failed:<analyzer>` (existing behavior).
- No Send button. Anywhere. Ever.

---

## Resolved decisions (coordinator)

```
embedding provider       same OpenAI-compat pattern as LLM · new env var EMBEDDING_MODEL
                         default to "mistral-embed" if user is on Mistral · fallback works for OpenAI
                         dimensions stored in env or detected at first call

chunking strategy        paragraph chunker (split on \n\n) · simple and good for Romanian SME docs
                         soft length: target 200-1000 chars per chunk · sentence-fallback if a paragraph
                         is too long · documents that are one paragraph stay one chunk
                         do NOT introduce sliding-window or hierarchical chunking yet

retrieval                pgvector cosine similarity · K=5 default · adjustable via env later
                         no reranking · no hybrid search · pure vector for slice-5

indexing as analyzer     DocumentIndexer is a registered Analyzer (applies_to=ALL · runs last)
                         no special-casing in the dispatcher · framework keeps its shape
                         idempotent: delete-by-document_id then insert · safe to re-run

ask endpoint shape       synchronous (not BackgroundTask) · user types, waits ~5-15s, sees answer
                         loading spinner in UI · timeout 30s
                         records PromptRun with document_id=null · prompt_name=ask_company · v1

draft reply as analyzer  DraftReplyGenerator follows the same Analyzer Protocol
                         applies_to={"client_request"} · runs after Indexer (so RAG context is available)
                         retrieves top-3 chunks from THE COMPANY'S OTHER DOCS (not the email itself)
                         to ground the reply in company knowledge
                         saves to analyzer_outputs.draft_reply_generator
                         frontend reads from there · falls back to hiding the panel if absent

OCR                      OUT of slice-5 · deferred until pilot user explicitly hits an image-only PDF
                         and asks for support · rationale: no signal yet · pdfplumber covers the
                         common case · adding OCR is its own infrastructure (Tesseract + image preprocess
                         + accuracy tuning) and shouldn't be paid for speculatively

pipeline hardening       FIRST task of slice-5 · ships the safety net before new code rides on it
                         outer try/except around run_analysis BackgroundTask body
                         catches Exception (not BaseException — let KeyboardInterrupt propagate)
                         writes audit event with truncated traceback (first 800 chars)
                         sets Document.status="failed" · keeps system available for next upload

seed expansion           7 → 8 docs (add email_client_apartament_bucuresti for Draft Reply)
                         remaining 8 slice-2 mock docs deferred · expand on pilot demand
                         all 8 seeded docs go through indexing in slice-5

eval thresholds          ask: source-citation correctness ≥80% · keyword presence ≥70%
                         draft: human_review_required must be true · score ≥7 · zero commitments
                         these can be tuned after first eval pass · note in patchlog
```

---

## Schema additions

```
new extension     CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;

new table         document_chunks
                    id              UUID PK
                    document_id     UUID FK → documents(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
                    chunk_index     INTEGER NOT NULL
                    content         TEXT NOT NULL
                    embedding       VECTOR(<dim>)   -- dim from EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS env
                    metadata        JSONB
                    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()

new index         CREATE INDEX document_chunks_embedding_idx
                    ON document_chunks USING hnsw (embedding vector_cosine_ops);
                    -- ivfflat acceptable if hnsw not available; record choice in patchlog
```

