3. CHUNKING + EMBEDDINGS SERVICES.
   - apps/api/app/services/chunking.py: chunk_paragraph(text: str) -> list[str]. Split on r"\n\s*\n", trim, drop empty. If a chunk exceeds ~1000 chars, split further on sentence boundaries (regex on .!? followed by whitespace). Return chunks in document order.
   - apps/api/app/services/embeddings.py: provider adapter using openai SDK with custom base_url (env: EMBEDDING_MODEL, EMBEDDING_API_BASE_URL or fallback to LLM_API_BASE_URL). Functions: embed(text: str) -> list[float]; embed_batch(texts: list[str]) -> list[list[float]]. Do NOT import openai outside this module.
   - Add EMBEDDING_MODEL and EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS to .env.example with a Mistral default (e.g., "mistral-embed", 1024) AND OpenAI alternative as comments.
   - Note: the configured EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS must match the VECTOR(N) column you migrated; if you guessed differently, drop and recreate the column or run another migration.
   Commit: "slice-5(rag): chunking + embeddings provider adapter"

4. DOCUMENT INDEXER ANALYZER.
   - apps/api/app/analyzers/document_indexer.py: class DocumentIndexer implementing the Protocol. applies_to = set of ALL DocType values. run() chunks document.raw_text, embeds in batch, then atomically deletes any existing chunks for this document and inserts fresh ones. Returns AnalyzerResult with parsed_output={"chunk_count": N}.
   - Register in registry.ANALYZERS as the LAST entry (after content analyzers so it indexes any merged context, though for slice-5 it only indexes raw_text — keeping order future-proof).
   - merge.py: handle DocumentIndexer's result by storing parsed_output into analyzer_outputs (no scalar columns to update).
   Commit: "slice-5(indexer): DocumentIndexer registered last · idempotent re-indexing"

5. RETRIEVAL HELPER.
   - apps/api/app/services/retrieval.py: top_k(query_embedding: list[float], k: int = 5) -> list[ChunkHit]. ChunkHit = {chunk_id, document_id, filename, content, score}. Pure SQL using pgvector cosine operator <=>; ORDER BY embedding <=> :query_embedding LIMIT :k.
   - Optional: filter by document_id-list parameter (for Draft Reply scoping later).
   Commit: "slice-5(rag): retrieval top_k helper"

6. ASK MY COMPANY (LIVE).
   - apps/api/app/prompts/ask_company_v1.txt: first line "# prompt: ask_company v1", body VERBATIM from codocz §19.19. Substitute {{USER_QUESTION}} and {{RETRIEVED_CONTEXT}} placeholders.
